Each target region's cells on the device are bumped from chunks of its own,
in the slot that the host gives it, which the host frees as the region ends
(docs/INPROGRESS.md, The device's side of the first slice, step 6). Here a
GPU process waits while 40 regions run, each making about 3 MB of cells,
some in the teams of a loop, so no moment comes when nothing runs on the
device. With the arenas limited to 32 MiB, the regions run only if each
region's chunks go when it ends; with 2 MiB, less than one region needs,
the program stops.
REQUIRES: amdgpu-gpu

RUN: merkc -fopenmp -fdo-loops -fprocess-declarations --offload-arch=%offload-arch %libomp-flags %S/Inputs/region-arena-beside-process.m -o %t
RUN: %gpu-env OMP_TARGET_OFFLOAD=MANDATORY MERK_DEVICE_ARENA_BYTES=33554432 MERK_CHECK_DEVICE_MEMORY=1 timeout -k 1 120 %t 2>&1 | FileCheck %s --match-full-lines --strict-whitespace
RUN: merkc -O2 -fopenmp -fdo-loops -fprocess-declarations --offload-arch=%offload-arch %libomp-flags %S/Inputs/region-arena-beside-process.m -o %t.O2
RUN: %gpu-env OMP_TARGET_OFFLOAD=MANDATORY MERK_DEVICE_ARENA_BYTES=33554432 MERK_CHECK_DEVICE_MEMORY=1 timeout -k 1 120 %t.O2 2>&1 | FileCheck %s --match-full-lines --strict-whitespace
CHECK:200006200000
CHECK-NEXT:7
CHECK-NEXT:Mercury runtime: 0 chunks of the devices' arenas and 0 rings are allocated

RUN: not %gpu-env OMP_TARGET_OFFLOAD=MANDATORY MERK_DEVICE_ARENA_BYTES=2097152 timeout -k 1 120 %t.O2 2>&1 | FileCheck %s --check-prefix=FULL
FULL: Mercury runtime: the devices' arenas are full: see MERK_DEVICE_ARENA_BYTES
